.SH "NAME"
git-autosquash \- Automatically squash git changes back into historical commits
.
.SH "SYNOPSIS"
.nf
\fIgit autosquash\fR [\-\-line\-by\-line] [\-i | \-\-interactive] [\-n | \-\-dry\-run]
                 [\-\-source <source>] [\-\-base <base>] [\-v | \-\-verbose]
.fi
.
.SH "DESCRIPTION"
.PP
\fBgit autosquash\fR squashes uncommitted changes (from working directory or index) back into their logical source commits\&. It analyzes each hunk using git blame to determine which historical commit originally added the modified lines\&.
.PP
The tool operates in two modes:
.RS 4
.PP
\fBInteractive mode\fR (\-i/\-\-interactive): Launches a TUI (Text User Interface) for manual review and approval of each hunk before squashing\&.
.PP
\fBAutomatic mode\fR (default): Automatically squashes all hunks without user interaction\&.
.RE
.PP
git-autosquash uses a split-commit approach combined with git's 3-way merge algorithm for reliable hunk application\&. This handles complex cases like removing lines from the commit that originally added them, which patch-based approaches cannot handle\&.
.PP
Validation mechanisms prevent data corruption:
.RS 4
.PP
\fBSourceNormalizer\fR: Converts all input sources (working-tree, index, HEAD, commits) to a single commit before processing\&.
.PP
\fBProcessingValidator\fR: Performs pre-flight and post-flight validation using \fIgit diff\fR to ensure no data loss\&.
.RE
.
.SH "OPTIONS"
.PP
\fB\-\-line\-by\-line\fR
.RS 4
Use line-by-line hunk splitting instead of default git hunks\&. This creates one hunk per changed line, allowing more granular control over which changes are squashed where\&.
.RE
.PP
\fB\-i\fR, \fB\-\-interactive\fR
.RS 4
Launch interactive TUI for manual hunk review and approval\&. The TUI displays each hunk with its target commit and allows you to approve, ignore, or modify the target for each change\&.
.RE
.PP
\fB\-n\fR, \fB\-\-dry\-run\fR
.RS 4
Show what would be done without making any changes to the repository\&.
.RE
.PP
\fB\-\-source\fR <source>
.RS 4
Specify what to process\&. Options:
.RS 4
.PP
\fBauto\fR (default): Automatically detect based on repository status (working-tree, index, or HEAD)
.PP
\fBworking\-tree\fR: Process unstaged changes in the working directory
.PP
\fBindex\fR: Process staged changes in the index
.PP
\fBhead\fR: Process the HEAD commit
.PP
\fB<commit-sha>\fR: Process a specific commit by SHA
.RE
.PP
When \fBhead\fR or a commit SHA is specified, git blame analysis starts on <commit>~1 (the parent commit)\&.
.RE
.PP
\fB\-\-base\fR <base>
.RS 4
Specify the base commit or branch for merge-base calculation\&. Use this when working on feature branches that are not based on main/master\&. Examples: \-\-base andrewleech/usbd_net or \-\-base origin/develop\&.
.RE
.PP
\fB\-v\fR, \fB\-\-verbose\fR
.RS 4
Enable verbose debug output for troubleshooting\&. Shows detailed information about hunk processing, blame analysis, and rebase operations\&.
.RE
.PP
\fB\-\-install\-completion\fR
.RS 4
Install shell completion for the current shell\&.
.RE
.PP
\fB\-\-show\-completion\fR
.RS 4
Show completion script for the current shell, allowing manual installation or customization\&.
.RE
.PP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
.RS 4
Show help message and exit\&.
.RE
.
.SH "EXAMPLES"
.PP
Review and squash all uncommitted changes interactively:
.RS 4
.nf
$ git autosquash \-i
.fi
.RE
.PP
Automatically squash all changes without review (default):
.RS 4
.nf
$ git autosquash
.fi
.RE
.PP
Preview what would be squashed without making changes:
.RS 4
.nf
$ git autosquash \-n
.fi
.RE
.PP
Interactively review in dry-run mode:
.RS 4
.nf
$ git autosquash \-i \-n
.fi
.RE
.PP
Squash a specific commit back into its sources:
.RS 4
.nf
$ git autosquash \-\-source abc123
.fi
.RE
.PP
Use line-by-line splitting for granular control:
.RS 4
.nf
$ git autosquash \-i \-\-line\-by\-line
.fi
.RE
.PP
Work on a feature branch with custom base:
.RS 4
.nf
$ git autosquash \-i \-\-base origin/develop
.fi
.RE
.PP
Debug with verbose output:
.RS 4
.nf
$ git autosquash \-v \-i
.fi
.RE
.
.SH "HOW IT WORKS"
.PP
git-autosquash follows a 6-step process:
.PP
.B 1. Source Normalization
.RS 4
All input sources (working-tree, index, HEAD, commits) are normalized to a single commit using SourceNormalizer\&. Temporary commits are created with \-\-no\-verify for working-tree and index sources\&.
.RE
.PP
.B 2. Commit Splitting
.RS 4
HunkCommitSplitter splits the source commit into separate temporary commits, one per hunk\&. Each split commit contains exactly one change and is stored on a temporary branch\&.
.RE
.PP
.B 3. Blame Analysis
.RS 4
For each hunk, git blame determines which historical commit originally added the lines being modified\&. The BlameAnalysisEngine handles complex cases and provides fallback options when blame fails\&.
.RE
.PP
.B 4. Interactive Review (if \-i flag used)
.RS 4
The TUI displays each hunk with its target commit, allowing approval, ignore, or target modification\&. FileConsistencyTracker ensures hunks from the same file use consistent targets\&.
.RE
.PP
.B 5. Cherry-Pick Application
.RS 4
For each approved hunk, RebaseManager cherry-picks its split commit using \fIgit cherry\-pick \-\-no\-commit\fR\&. Git's 3-way merge handles complex cases automatically\&. Falls back to patch-based approach only if split-commit fails\&.
.RE
.PP
.B 6. Validation
.RS 4
ProcessingValidator performs post-flight validation using \fIgit diff <start> <end>\fR to ensure no data corruption occurred during the squashing process\&.
.RE
.
.SH "VALIDATION AND SAFETY"
.PP
Safety mechanisms:
.PP
\fBPre-flight validation\fR: Validates hunk counts match expectations before processing\&.
.PP
\fBPost-flight validation\fR: Uses \fIgit diff\fR to compare the starting and ending repository states, ensuring no data loss or corruption\&.
.PP
\fBReflog tracking\fR: All rebase operations are tracked in git reflog with descriptive messages\&.
.PP
\fBConflict handling\fR: If conflicts occur during squashing, the tool pauses and provides instructions for resolution or abort\&.
.PP
\fBTemporary commit cleanup\fR: All temporary commits and branches created during processing are automatically removed upon completion\&.
.
.SH "EXIT STATUS"
.PP
.B 0
.RS 4
Successful completion\&. All hunks were squashed (or would be squashed in dry-run mode) without errors\&.
.RE
.PP
.B 1
.RS 4
Error occurred\&. This could be due to validation failures, git operation errors, or user abort\&.
.RE
.
.SH "ENVIRONMENT"
.PP
\fBGIT_DIR\fR
.RS 4
Path to the .git directory\&. Used by git operations\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBGIT_WORK_TREE\fR
.RS 4
Path to the working tree\&. Used by git operations\&.
.RE
.
.SH "FILES"
.PP
\fB.git/rebase-merge/\fR
.RS 4
Temporary directory used during interactive rebase operations\&. Contains state for paused/continuing rebases\&.
.RE
.PP
\fB.git/ORIG_HEAD\fR
.RS 4
Backup of HEAD before rebase operations\&. Used for recovery if needed\&.
.RE
.
